# SibylFS scripts the model allows on ext4 and rejects through dcfs
# (guest/sibylfs.sh), one per line, each with the reason above it.
#
# lseek(dirfd, 0, SEEK_END) and lseek(dirfd, -2000, SEEK_END) on a directory:
# ext4's directory llseek (ext4_dir_llseek, fs/ext4/dir.c) takes the end of a
# hashed directory to be its largest hash offset, and answers EOVERFLOW, which
# is what the model says. A FUSE directory uses generic_file_llseek
# (fs/fuse/dir.c), whose end is the directory's st_size: the kernel answers
# 4096 and 2096 without a request to dcfs. No file system under dcfs can
# change that; xfs and btrfs answer as FUSE does (their lists are empty: the
# model rejects the backing file system there too).
